# Databases + text caches (golden / RL)

## Three stores (do not conflate)

| Store | Path / env | Role |
|-------|------------|------|
| **Local SQLite** | `cannabis_papers.db` or `--sqlite-path` | Dev + golden cycle after `DATABASE_URL` is popped |
| **Fly volume SQLite** | `/data/cannabis_papers.db` | Populated production-like SQLite on the app VM |
| **Postgres** | `DATABASE_URL` | Live Fly Postgres; pull/push only |

Empty `/app/cannabis_papers.db` is **not** the corpus. Always pass a populated `--sqlite-path` (local `cannabis_papers.db` after pull, or `/data/cannabis_papers.db` on Fly).

## Why golden pops `DATABASE_URL`

`scripts/golden_endpoint_cycle.py` pops `DATABASE_URL` so LLM / promote / guard / reingest hit **SQLite** (`DATABASE_PATH`), not Postgres. Pull/push briefly restore `DATABASE_URL`. Never assume default empty SQLite has candidate papers — pull first or point `--sqlite-path` at a populated DB.

## PDF / text cache reuse (avoid re-download)

| Cache | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Paper text/PDF | `scratch/paper_cache/` (`text/`, `pdfs/`, `meta/`) — override with `PAPER_TEXT_CACHE_DIR` |
| Golden candidate blobs | `scratch/golden_dataset/tree_path_golden.json` |
| Confirmed text | `scratch/golden_dataset/golden_confirmed.json` |

`paper_text_cache.resolve_paper_text` prefers disk cache over HTTP. Force reuse-only: `SKIP_PDF_FETCH=1`. Optional LLM cache fill: `GOLDEN_LLM_FETCH_PDF=1`.

## Golden gate

- Endpoint-scoped guard only (`--endpoint-id`).
- Limited reingest (`GOLDEN_FULL_SUBNODE_REINGEST=0`), not full corpus.
- `node2a.clinical_observational.inhaled` cleared ≥90% (July 2026, build `20260711-node2a-golden-obs-inhaled-v2`) — **Loop A perpetual is allowed**.
- Golden rows remain **gated** (one at a time, no `AUTO_ADVANCE`); see `.cursor/rules/golden-endpoint-policy.mdc`.
